    "explanation": "From the rows checked, the August-December decline was -4.44M of Revenue, which matches 95.9% of the full-year decline in the scan evidence. The drop is concentrated in a few areas rather than being broad-based: by department, CONSUMER GOODS fell -1.56M, TECHNOLOGY -1.35M and LIFESTYLE -1.24M; by section, PERSONAL CARE fell -772K, CONSUMER DEVICES -722K, ENTERTAINMENTS -626K, HOME TEXTILES -543K and PROVISIONS -540K. At category level, the largest declines were LED TV -582K, BLANKET DOUBLE -401K, TORCHES -356K, ROASTED NUTS ROASTERY -343K and FRESH MUTTON OTHER -290K, with October already flagged as led by LED TV and BLANKET DOUBLE, so the period decline is likely associated with weakness in a small set of technology, home and consumer-goods categories rather than a uniform slowdown across all categories. Units also fell in most of those same categories and sections, which is consistent with softer demand or mix pressure rather than a pure pricing effect, although this model cannot prove cause. One important caveat: 111.6K of the decline sits in unassigned merchandise rows with blank department, section and category, so merchandise breakdowns do not cover the full business cleanly. Best follow-up check: review the month-by-month category trend for LED TV and BLANKET DOUBLE, especially October and August, to see whether the decline was a one-month step-down or a sustained loss across the period.",
